  "worked_solution": "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\u0394x,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+k\u0394x$ with $\u0394x=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=5$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=6,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\n\u0394x=\\frac{6-1}{5}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\u0394x & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+k\u0394x)\u0394x \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{5-1}f(1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}f(1+k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}\\frac{6}{1+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
